WEBVTT

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:30.976
(Laughter)

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:32.976
I'll stand up too, and --

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:34.976
(Laughter)

00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:37.976
(Applause)

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:39.976
They have to say that.

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:41.976
They had to be very cautious.

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:44.143
But what I'm saying is,
you can be delighted,

00:27:44.167 --> 00:27:46.976
because the editor
of Science, who is no dummy,

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.976
and both of these fairly professional --

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.976
really professional teams, have
really come to the same conclusion

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:54.976
and in the bottom lines in their papers

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:57.000
they have to say, what this means
is, that what we've been thinking,

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:00.239
was the global circulation
model that we predict